  "slug": "vitreous-centimeter-b971",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend PSC-derived models to new tissues (vitreous, olfactory epithelium) and benchmark fidelity across heart organoid protocols and cell systems.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the expansion and benchmarking of in vitro developmental models built from pluripotent or embryonic cells. New tissue targets appear. Centimeter-scale human vitreous organoids were derived via TGF-beta signaling and mirror human vitreous structure. Human iPSC-derived olfactory sensory organoids show neuronal and glial diversity, maturation signatures matching fetal nasal tissue, and network bursting. In embryology, mouse zygotes were cultured continuously ex utero to early organogenesis after BMP inhibition and culture optimization, forming axes and organ primordia. Fidelity assessment is a parallel theme. An integrated single-cell atlas of 16 heart organoid datasets benchmarks developmental fidelity across protocols. Transcriptomic aging readouts in iPSC-derived neurons were used to test eight candidate geroprotectors, with mTORC1 and MEK-ERK pathways identified as tunable. Two adjacent studies apply these platforms in other settings. One is a TSPAN10 knockout in hESC-derived RPE affecting pigmentation, polarity and antioxidant defence. The other profiles bovine MSCs across culture systems for cultivated meat.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
